 Controlled by: DEPARTMENT OF THE NAVY&nbsp; 

 Controlled by: NAVAIR&nbsp; 

 CUI Category: General Procurement and Acquisition and Source Selection&nbsp; 

 Distribution/Dissemination Control: FEDCON&nbsp; 

 POC: PCO, faith.l.lagore.civ@us.navy.mil&nbsp; 

 Sources Sought RFI Synopsis: Labor-Only Fire Alarm System Support Services&nbsp;&nbsp; 

 THIS IS A REQUEST FOR INFORMATION (RFI) ONLY. The responses to this sources sought will be utilized to determine if the Government will determine what the vendor capability and the potential cost of the services requested.&nbsp; 

 The Product Service Code (PSC) for this requirement is J063. The North American Industry Classification System (NAICS) code is 561621.&nbsp; 

 SCOPE OF WORK:&nbsp;&nbsp; 

 &nbsp; 
Labor-Only Fire Alarm System Support Services&nbsp; 
&nbsp; 

 1. Purpose&nbsp; 
Provide labor-only technical support for the maintenance, programming, troubleshooting, repair, modification, testing, and commissioning of Fire Alarm Systems (FAS) installed at NAWS China Lake. Parts shall be furnished by the Government after receiving itemized quote from the Contractor. The Government will not provide tools, test equipment, computers, software, or any other materials required to perform the work.&nbsp; 

 2. Quantity of Services&nbsp; 
The contract will include a maximum of thirty (30) on-site service calls during the period of performance.&nbsp; 



	 Up to three (3) of these calls may be designated as emergency service calls requiring a response time of 24 hours or less.&nbsp; 





	 All other service calls shall require a response within 72 hours.&nbsp; 





	 Additional service calls may be ordered at the same unit price as needed.&nbsp; 



 3. Definition of a Service Call&nbsp; 
A service call consists of one on-site visit by the Contractor to perform up to eight (8) hours of productive work. Travel time is excluded and will not be paid. The Government will prioritize and bundle multiple work requests into single service calls whenever practical.&nbsp; 

 4. Contractor Qualifications&nbsp; 



	 All technicians performing work under this contract shall hold current NICET Level II or higher certification in Fire Alarm Systems.&nbsp; 





	 The Contractor must be factory-authorized and possess all required proprietary software, programming tools, licenses, dongles, and access rights for the full range of fire alarm systems currently installed at NAWS China Lake (including legacy systems). Systems include but are not limited to:&nbsp; 
	Edwards (EST), Fike, Potter, Bosch/Radionics, Honeywell, Siemens (Cerberus), Mircom, Gamewell-FCI, Notifier, Simplex, Kidde, Monaco Enterprises, Fire-Lite, and Autocall.&nbsp; 



 5. Scope of Services&nbsp; 
Examples of services to be provided upon request by the Government include but are not limited to:&nbsp; 



	 Troubleshooting, programming changes, and system modifications&nbsp; 





	 Commissioning and retro-commissioning of fire alarm systems&nbsp; 





	 100% zone testing coordinated with the Regional Dispatch Center (RDC)&nbsp; 





	 Account activations with RDC&nbsp; 





	 Completion and updating of R9 forms with RDC&nbsp; 





	 Technical telephone support during normal business hours&nbsp; 





	 Repair and restoration of systems to normal operating condition&nbsp; 





	 Modifying, correcting, or replacing obsolete systems.&nbsp; 





	 Software and hardware technical assistance&nbsp; 



 6. Reporting Requirements&nbsp; 
For each service call, the Contractor shall provide a detailed Field Service Report that includes, at a minimum:&nbsp; 



	 Service Call Number&nbsp; 





	 Date(s) of service&nbsp; 





	 Invoice Number&nbsp; 





	 Navy Point of Contact&nbsp; 





	 Technician name(s)&nbsp; 





	 Building number(s)&nbsp; 





	 Description of work requested by the Navy&nbsp; 





	 Detailed description of actions taken and resolution&nbsp; 





	 Relevant tracking notes (delays, cancellations, parts required, etc.)&nbsp; 



 If a service call is not fully resolved during the visit, the report must also include:&nbsp; 



	 Reason the repair was not performed&nbsp; 





	 Remaining actions required to complete the repair (including specific parts needed)&nbsp; 





	 Estimated additional labor hours and projected completion date&nbsp; 



 7. Invoicing&nbsp; 
Invoices shall be submitted for each completed service call and shall reference the service call number. Each invoice must be accompanied by the corresponding Field Service Report.&nbsp; 

 Classified material SHALL NOT be submitted. All proprietary or corporate data received shall be clearly identified and will be protected from release to sources outside the Government.  Any resulting contract is anticipated to have a security classification level of unclassified at time of contract award for personnel and facilities clearances.&nbsp; 

 Your response to this Sources Sought, including any capabilities statement, must be electronically submitted in either Microsoft Word or searchable Portable Documen
